3. `cbor_value_is_byte_string`
​ `cbor_value_is_byte_string()` is a simple type check for a `CborValue`. Use it to test whether the current value is a CBOR byte string before reading it as one. It returns `true` only when `value->type == CborByteStringType`, otherwise `false`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Strings */
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_byte_string(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
4. `cbor_value_get_next_byte`
​ Returns the parser cursor: the next unread byte in the CBOR input. Use it to inspect/peek where `CborValue` will read next. It simply returns `it->source.ptr`; no validation, side effects, or advancing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API const uint8_t *cbor_value_get_next_byte(const CborValue *it);
​ ```
5. `cbor_value_get_string_length`
​ Returns the length of a definite CBOR text/byte string. Use only after checking the value is a string; it asserts that. If the length is unknown, returns `CborErrorUnknownLength`. If it won’t fit in `size_t`, returns `CborErrorDataTooLarge`; otherwise `CborNoError`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API CborError cbor_value_get_string_length(const CborValue *value, size_t *length);
​ ```
6. `cbor_value_get_array_length`
​ Returns the length of a CBOR array when it’s known. Use only on array values; it asserts if `value` isn’t an array. If length is indefinite, it returns `CborErrorUnknownLength`. If the length won’t fit in `size_t`, it returns `CborErrorDataTooLarge`; otherwise `CborNoError`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API CborError cbor_value_get_array_length(const CborValue *value, size_t *length);
​ ```
7. `cbor_value_is_text_string`
​ Checks whether a `CborValue` currently points to a CBOR text string. Use it to test the item’s type before reading it as UTF-8 text. Returns `true` only when `value->type == CborTextStringType`; otherwise `false`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_text_string(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
8. `cbor_value_get_map_length`
​ Returns a map’s item count. Use only on a map `CborValue`; it asserts if not a map. If length is indefinite, returns `CborErrorUnknownLength`. On success writes `size_t` length; if it won’t fit, returns `CborErrorDataTooLarge`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API CborError cbor_value_get_map_length(const CborValue *value, size_t *length);
​ ```

