## Target API Functions

1. `cbor_value_is_simple_type`
​ `cbor_value_is_simple_type()` checks whether a `CborValue` currently represents a CBOR simple type. It’s a read-only predicate: returns `true` only when `value->type == CborSimpleType`, otherwise `false`. Use it to test before handling simple values.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Simple types */
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_simple_type(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
2. `cbor_value_is_null`
​ `cbor_value_is_null` is a tinycbor type-check helper. Use it with a valid `CborValue*` to test whether the current item is CBOR `null`. It returns `true` only when `value->type == CborNullType`; otherwise `false` (including undefined/other types).
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Null & undefined type */
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_null(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
3. `cbor_value_is_undefined`
​ Checks whether a `CborValue` is the CBOR `undefined` simple value. Use it on a valid `CborValue*`; it returns `true` only when `value->type == CborUndefinedType`, otherwise `false`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_undefined(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
4. `cbor_value_is_integer`
​ `cbor_value_is_integer()` is a simple type check: it returns true iff `value->type == CborIntegerType`. Use it to test whether a `CborValue` currently represents an integer before reading it as one. It doesn’t validate range or decode anything.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Integers */
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_integer(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
5. `cbor_value_get_simple_type`
​ Returns the CBOR “simple” value from a `CborValue`. Use only after confirming `cbor_value_is_simple_type(value)`. It asserts on invalid input, writes `value->extra` to `*result`, and returns `CborNoError`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API CborError cbor_value_get_simple_type(const CborValue *value, uint8_t *result);
​ ```
6. `cbor_value_is_tag`
​ `cbor_value_is_tag()` is a simple type check: it returns `true` when `value->type == CborTagType`, otherwise `false`. Use it to test whether a `CborValue` currently points to a CBOR tag before reading tag-specific data.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Tags */
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_tag(const CborValue *value);
​ ```

