​ ```
2. `cbor_value_get_string_length`
​ Returns the length of a definite CBOR text/byte string. Use only after checking the value is a string; it asserts that. If the length is unknown, returns `CborErrorUnknownLength`. If it won’t fit in `size_t`, returns `CborErrorDataTooLarge`; otherwise `CborNoError`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API CborError cbor_value_get_string_length(const CborValue *value, size_t *length);
​ ```
3. `cbor_value_string_iteration_at_end`
​ Checks whether string-chunk iteration is finished. Use it while iterating a CBOR text/byte string with chunk APIs. It returns `true` when `cbor_value_get_string_chunk_size()` reports `CborErrorNoMoreStringChunks`; otherwise `false`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_string_iteration_at_end(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
4. `cbor_value_begin_string_iteration`
​ Begins chunked iteration over a text/byte string `CborValue`. Use it only on a string value and only once before iterating chunks. It asserts on non-strings or if iteration is already active, then delegates to the internal iterator setup.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API CborError cbor_value_begin_string_iteration(CborValue *value);
​ ```
5. `cbor_value_is_text_string`
​ Checks whether a `CborValue` currently points to a CBOR text string. Use it to test the item’s type before reading it as UTF-8 text. Returns `true` only when `value->type == CborTextStringType`; otherwise `false`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_text_string(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
6. `cbor_value_is_valid`
​ `cbor_value_is_valid()` checks whether a `CborValue*` is non-NULL and not marked `CborInvalidType`. Use it as a quick guard before reading/advancing a CBOR value. It returns `false` for NULL or invalid values, `true` otherwise.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_valid(const CborValue *value);
​ ```

